  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The mass $M$ of a radioactive substance is initially $10\\text{ g}$ and $20$ years later its mass is $9.6\\text{ g}$. If the relationship between $M$ grams and $t$ years is of the form $M=M_0 10^{-kt}$, find:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$M_0$ and $k$. Give $k$ correct to four significant figures.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$M_0=10$, $k\\approx8.864\\times10^{-4}$.",
          "worked": "At $t=0$, the initial mass gives $M_0=10$.\n\nUsing $M=9.6$ when $t=20$:\n$$\\begin{align*}9.6&=10\\times10^{-20k}\\\\0.96&=10^{-20k}\\\\\\log_{10}(0.96)&=-20k\\\\k&=-\\frac{\\log_{10}(0.96)}{20}\\\\k&\\approx8.864\\times10^{-4}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the half-life of the radioactive substance, correct to two decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$339.59$ years.",
          "worked": "At the half-life, $M=\\frac12M_0$. Using the unrounded value $k=-\\frac{\\log_{10}(0.96)}{20}$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12&=10^{-kt}\\\\\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=-kt\\\\kt&=\\log_{10}2\\\\t&=\\frac{\\log_{10}2}{k}\\\\t&\\approx339.59\\text{ years}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
